# FusionPlant Digital Twin — environment template
#
# This project is a fully client-side simulation and currently requires NO
# credentials, API keys or backend configuration of any kind. Everything runs in
# the browser and no network requests are made at runtime.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING ANY VARIABLE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vite inlines every variable prefixed with VITE_ into the client bundle.
# Anything you put there is PUBLIC — visible to anyone who opens the deployed
# page or inspects the built JavaScript. Never place an API key, token, password
# or private endpoint in a VITE_ variable.
#
# If a future feature needs a secret (for example an LLM API key), do not call
# that service from the browser. Add a small backend or serverless proxy that
# holds the secret, and give the frontend only the proxy URL.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Copy this file to `.env.local` if you ever need local overrides:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
# `.env.local` is git-ignored.

# Optional: base path when hosting under a sub-directory (no secret).
# VITE_BASE_PATH=/

# Example of a non-secret runtime configuration value:
# VITE_PLANT_DISPLAY_NAME=FusionPlant Digital Twin

# Example of a secret that MUST NOT live here (kept only as documentation):
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=YOUR_API_KEY_HERE
